# Each turn loads the key from the list and calls one stub with the set and the key in registers. The answer is a boolean in the lowest bit: one mask, one branch.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[key]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[found]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[key]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@[[low]] = Trunc(b@[[found]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[bit]] = BitAnd(b@[[low]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[bit]], Terminal)
# The stub is declared to write the storage of arrays, so the storage and the length of the list are loaded again behind it, once.
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[again]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSObject_butterfly, {{*}})
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[again]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength, {{*}})
# LOOP-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub is the only call of the loop.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# The stub may write the length, which is read again on every turn: nothing counts the turns ahead of the loop, so the loop polls on each of them.
# CALLS-COUNT-2: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# Set.prototype.has cannot be replaced and nothing of the same name hides it on the object: the function does not read it by name, make its function object, or test the object or the function.
